        "answer": "# Monsoon in India\n\nMonsoons occur in India primarily due to **seasonal reversal winds**. India remains under the influence of these winds for a significant part of the year.\n\nSpecifically:\n1.  **Southwest Monsoon**: The onset of the southwest monsoon brings down temperatures across India and causes moderate to heavy rainfall. This happens even though the sun's rays are vertical over central India during mid-June, the summer season ends by the end of May due to this monsoon.\n2.  **Northeast Monsoon**: The climate of Southeast India is influenced by the northeast monsoon. \n\n**📘 Source:** Samacheer Kalvi Class 10 Social Science • Does Monsoon Occur"
